hadiths[180]{hadithnumber,text}:
"11777","Abu al-Darda (may Allah be pleased with him) reported that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that when Allah, Mighty and Majestic, created Adam, He struck his right shoulder and brought forth a white offspring like small ants, and struck his left shoulder and brought forth a black offspring like charred coal. He decreed their final abodes without need of any one. > **[""To those in His right: to Paradise, and I do not care; and to those in His left hand: to the Fire, and I do not care""]**"
"11778","Abu Nadrah reported that a Companion called Abu Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) was visited by his brothers during illness while he wept. They reminded him of the Prophet's (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) counsel to trim the mustache and remain steadfast till meeting him. He replied that he had also heard of the two handfuls and did not know in which he stood. > **[""Indeed Allah, Mighty and Majestic, took a handful in His right and the other in the other Hand, and said: this is for this, and this is for this, and I do not care""]**"
"11779","Abd al-Rahman ibn Qatadah al-Sulami (may Allah be pleased with him) said he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say that Allah created Adam, then took mankind from his back and assigned one group to Paradise and one to the Fire, without care. A questioner asked on what basis then to act, and he answered: according to the occurrences of decree. > **[""These are in Paradise, and I do not care, and these are in the Fire, and I do not care""]** > **[""Act according to the places of decree""]**"
"11780","Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said Allah took a handful and assigned it to Paradise by His mercy, and took another handful and assigned it to the Fire, without care. > **[""Indeed Allah took a handful and said: for Paradise by My mercy; and He took a handful and said: for the Fire, and I do not care""]**"
"11781","Abu Musa al-Ashari (may Allah be pleased with him) reported from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that when Allah, Blessed and Exalted, created Adam, He took two handfuls from his clay, one in His right and one in the other Hand, assigned them to Paradise and the Fire without care, then returned them to Adam's loins where they continue to reproduce till now. > **[""These to Paradise, and I do not care; and these to the Fire, and I do not care""]**"
"11782","Abu Said al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) reported from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning the two handfuls that one is appointed for Paradise and the other for the Fire, without care on Allah's part. > **[""This is in Paradise, and I do not care, and this is in the Fire, and I do not care""]**"
"11783","Abdullah ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) reported from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning the two handfuls that one group is for one abode and the other for the other. The narrator added that people then dispersed while not disputing concerning decree. > **[""These are for this, and these are for this""]**"
"11784","Hisham ibn Hakim ibn Hizam (may Allah be pleased with him) reported that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked whether deeds are begun anew or the decree is already decided. The Prophet answered that Allah took Adam's offspring from his back, made them witness over themselves, scattered them in His two Hands, assigned groups to Paradise and Fire, and facilitated each for its deeds. > **[""Indeed Allah, Blessed and Exalted, took the offspring of Adam from his back, then made them witness over themselves, then scattered them in His two Hands, and said: these in Paradise and these in the Fire; as for the people of Paradise, they are facilitated for the deeds of Paradise, and the people of the Fire are facilitated for the deeds of the Fire""]**"
"11785","Muadh ibn Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him), when death approached, wept. Asked why, he swore it was not panic of death nor grief for the world left behind, but fear from what he heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the two handfuls, not knowing in which he was. > **[""They are only two handfuls: a handful in the Fire and a handful in Paradise""]**"
"11786","Muawiyah (may Allah be pleased with him), who narrated little from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), reported that Allah brought forth Adam's offspring from his loins until they filled the earth. The transmitter Jafar illustrated their multitude by clasping his hands together. > **[""Indeed Allah, Majestic and Mighty, brought forth the offspring of Adam from his loins until they filled the earth""]**"
"11787","Abdullah ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) reported that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out, spread his right palm and then his left, announcing a written record from Allah, the Most Merciful, containing the names of the people of Paradise and of the Fire, with their fathers, tribes and clans, neither increased nor diminished. > **[""In the Name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful: this is a book from Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful, with the names of the people of Paradise and the names of their fathers, tribes and clans; nothing shall be added among them nor diminished from them""]** > **[""In the Name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful: this is a book from the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful, for the people of the Fire, with their names and the names of their fathers, tribes and clans; nothing shall be added among them nor diminished from them""]**"
"11788","Abdullah ibn Busr (may Allah be pleased with him) reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed them, spreading then closing his right hand for the people of Paradise and his left for the people of the Fire, with names, fathers and tribes fixed till Resurrection. He explained that a happy one may travel the wretched path till thought one of them, then happiness overtakes him, and vice versa, for each is facilitated. > **[""The people of Paradise with their names and the names of their fathers and tribes; nothing shall be added among them nor diminished till the Day of Resurrection""]** > **[""The people of Hell with their names and the names of their fathers and tribes; nothing shall be added among them nor diminished till the Day of Resurrection""]** > **[""Each is facilitated for what he was created for""]**"
"11789","Al-Bara ibn Azib (may Allah be pleased with him) reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) once came with two scrolls in his hands while looking at them. His Companions noted that Allah's Prophet is unlettered, neither reading nor writing. He drew near, spread the one in his right for Paradise and the like for the Fire. > **[""In the Name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful: this is a book from the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful, with the names of the people of Paradise and the names of their fathers and clans, summed against them; nothing shall be added at its end; your Lord has finished""]**"
"11790","Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) reported that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said Allah created Paradise and its people with clans and tribes, and the Fire and its people likewise, neither increased nor diminished. When asked why then act, he commanded action, for each is facilitated. > **[""Indeed Allah has created Paradise and created for it a people with their clans and tribes; nothing shall be added among them nor diminished; and He created the Fire and created for it a people with their clans and tribes; nothing shall be added among them nor diminished""]** > **[""Act, for each is facilitated for what he was created for""]**"
"11791","Abdullah ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) said he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say this clan of Quraysh would remain secure until near kinsmen turn them from their religion. A man of Quraysh asked whether he was in Paradise or Fire, and was told Paradise; another asked and was told Fire. Then he commanded silence. > **[""This clan of Quraysh shall remain secure until those equal in kinship turn them away from their religion""]** > **[""In Paradise""]** > **[""In the Fire""]** > **[""Remain silent toward me as long as I remain silent toward you; were it not that you would abandon burying one another, I would inform you of your marked ones among the people of the Fire so you would recognize them at death""]**"
"11792","Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out angry and addressed the people, saying they would not ask anything that day but he would inform them, while they sensed Jibril was with him. Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) pleaded that they were fresh from ignorance and asked pardon lest their faults be exposed. > **[""You will not ask me about anything today except that I inform you of it""]**"
"11793","Abdullah ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) reported from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, took the covenant from Adam's back at Numan on the Day of Arafah, brought forth every seed He would create, scattered them before Him, addressed them directly, and established the proof lest they claim heedlessness or blame ancestral idolatry. > **[""Am I not your Lord? They said: Yes, we bear witness; lest you say on the Day of Resurrection: indeed we were heedless of this; or you say: our fathers associated partners before, and we were offspring after them, so will You destroy us for what the falsifiers did""]**"
"11794","Abu Umamah al-Bahili (may Allah be pleased with him) reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said Allah created creation, settled the decree, took the covenant of the Prophets while His Throne was upon water, took the people of the right in His right and the wretched in His left, though both Hands of the Merciful are right. After mixing them and answering their question, he taught that Paradise folk do Paradise deeds and Fire folk do Fire deeds, and when Umar asked whether deeds are innovated or finished, he commanded action. > **[""O people of the right""]** > **[""Here we are at Your service and happiness is from You""]** > **[""Am I not your Lord? They said: Yes""]** > **[""Each people works for what they were created for; the people of Paradise work the deeds of Paradise, and the people of the Fire work the deeds of Fire""]** > **[""Act, for each is facilitated for what he was created for""]**"
"11795","Abdullah ibn Jafar (may Allah be pleased with them both) reported that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seated him behind him on the mount and addressed him as a youth, offering beneficial words: guard Allah, ask Allah alone, seek help from Allah alone, know the Pen has dried, creation cannot harm what was not written against him, and patience brings victory. > **[""O lad, shall I not grant you? Shall I not teach you words by which Allah will benefit you? Guard Allah, He will guard you; guard Allah, you will find Him before you; when you ask, ask Allah; when you seek help, seek help from Allah; know that the Pen has dried concerning what shall be; know that if creatures intended you harm not written against you, they could not overpower you; know that victory comes with patience, relief with distress, and ease with hardship""]**"
"11796","Abdullah ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said the first thing Allah created was the Pen, and He commanded it to write everything. > **[""Indeed the first thing Allah created was the Pen, and He commanded it to write everything""]**"
"11797","Abdullah ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) reported from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that when Allah created the Pen He said Write, and it flowed with all that shall be till the establishment of the Hour. > **[""Write""]**"
"11798","Hibban ibn Ubaydillah ibn Zuhayr al-Basri said he asked al-Dahhak ibn Muzahim about three verses on calamity prerecorded, deeds transcribed, and all things by measure. He answered with Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that Allah created the Throne then the Pen vast as heaven and earth, commanded it to flow with rain, plants, souls, deeds, provision and terms till Resurrection in the guarded hidden Book under the Throne; angels copy each year on Laylat al-Qadr in Ramadan what shall occur, review with guardian angels every Thursday eve finding no excess or loss; and each creature is fitted with suitable form and provision, as camel, land and sea animals and birds. > **[""With what, my Lord, shall I flow? With what I am creating and what shall be in My creation of rain, plants, souls, traces meaning deeds, provision, or term""]**"
"11799","Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) said he wished a denier of decree were present to strike his head, then described the Preserved Tablet of white pearl with red ruby edges, its pen and writing of light, vast as heaven and earth, which Allah regards three hundred and sixty times daily, creating, giving life and death, honor and humiliation, doing what He wills. > **[""Indeed Allah created a Preserved Tablet of white pearl, its two edges of red ruby, its pen of light and its writing of light, its breadth as between heaven and earth; He looks into it three hundred and sixty times each day, with each regard creating, giving life, causing death, honoring, humiliating, and doing what He wills""]**"
"11800","Marthad (may Allah be pleased with him), a Companion of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), said Allah drew two lines in His Book, then lifted the Pen, writing creation in one and what creation shall do in the other. > **[""Allah drew two lines in His Book, then lifted the Pen, and wrote in one of them creation, and wrote in the other what creation shall do""]**"
"11801","Al-Hasan ibn Ali (may Allah be pleased with them both) said the Book has been lifted, the Pen has dried, and matters stand decreed in a Book long past. > **[""The Book has been lifted, the Pen has dried, and matters stand by decree in a Book long past""]**"
"11802","Jundub ibn Abdillah and others (may Allah be pleased with them) reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said Adam and Musa disputed. Musa reproached Adam for being created by Allah's Hand, honored by angels and Paradise, then bringing people out of Paradise. Adam replied that Musa, spoken to privately and given the Torah, blamed him for a matter written upon him before his creation. So Adam overcame Musa. > **[""You are Musa whom Allah addressed intimately and gave the Torah; do you blame me for a matter decreed upon me before He created me""]** > **[""So Adam overcame Musa""]**"
"11803","In another narration Adam (peace be upon him) answered Musa by asking which is prior: himself or the written remembrance in the Preserved Tablet. > **[""Am I prior, or is the Remembrance prior""]**"
"11804","Abu Said al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) reported that Adam and Musa (peace be upon them both) disputed. Musa said Allah created Adam by His Hand, breathed His spirit into him, commanded angels to prostrate, housed him in Paradise, yet he lured people out. Adam answered that Allah chose Musa for messengership, sent the Torah and favored him, yet he blamed a matter Allah decreed before his creation. So Adam overcame Musa. > **[""O Adam, Allah created you by His Hand, breathed into you of His spirit, commanded the angels and they prostrated to you, and housed you in His Paradise, then you lured people and brought them out of Paradise""]** > **[""O Musa, Allah chose you with His message, sent down upon you the Torah, and did for you such and such; do you blame me for a matter Allah decreed upon me before He created me""]**"
"11805","Abdullah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both) reported that while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spoke at the doors of the chambers, Abu Bakr and Umar came with disputing groups. One man explained Abu Bakr held good deeds are from Allah and evil from servants, while Umar held both from Allah. The Prophet asked each to repeat, then swore to judge as Israfil judged between Jibril and Mikail, the first creation to discuss it, whose dispute was likewise referred to Israfil, who judged all decree good evil sweet bitter from Allah. > **[""What speech did I just hear, some answering others and refuting others""]** > **[""How did you state it""]** > **[""By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, I shall judge between you with the judgment of Israfil between Jibril and Mikail; they, by Him in Whose Hand is my soul, are the first of Allah's creation to discuss it; Mikail held the view of Abu Bakr, and Jibril held the view of Umar, so Jibril said to Mikail: whenever heaven folk differ, earth folk differ, so let us seek Israfil as judge; so they sought him and he judged between them with the reality of decree, its good and evil, sweet and bitter, all from Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and I judge between you likewise""]** > **[""O Abu Bakr, indeed Allah, Blessed and Exalted, had He willed not to be disobeyed, He would not have created Iblis""]**"
"11806","Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said when the drop rests in the womb forty days and forty nights, Allah sends an angel who asks about its term, sex, and misery or happiness, and is informed. > **[""O Lord, what is his term? O Lord, male or female? O Lord, wretched or happy""]**"
"11807","Abdullah ibn Masud (may Allah be pleased with him) reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said the drop stays forty days unchanged, then becomes a clot, then a lump, then bones likewise; when Allah wills to fashion him, He sends an angel who asks about sex, misery, stature, defect, strength, term, health, and all is written. Asked why act when finished, he commanded action, for each shall be directed. > **[""O Lord, male or female? Wretched or happy? Short or tall? Deficient or complete? His strength? His term? Sound or sick? So all that is written""]** > **[""Act, for each shall be directed to what he was created for""]**"
"11808","Abdullah ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said when Allah wills to create a soul, the angel of wombs inquires whether male or female, wretched or happy, Allah decrees, then writes between his eyes all he shall meet, even a stumble. > **[""O Lord, male or female? O Lord, wretched or happy""]**"
"11809","Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) reported from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that the wretched is he made wretched in his mother's belly, and the happy is he made happy in her belly. > **[""The wretched is he who was made wretched in his mother's belly, and the happy is he who was made happy in her belly""]**"
"11810","Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her) reported from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that when Allah, Blessed and Exalted, wills to create, He sends an angel into the womb who asks about boy or girl, misery, term, traits and provision, and everything is created with him in the womb. > **[""O Lord, what shall it be? O Lord, wretched or happy? O Lord, what is his term? What are his traits? O Lord, what is his provision? O Lord, what is his character""]**"
"11811","Abdullah ibn Masud (may Allah be pleased with him) reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said Allah, Glorious in remembrance, created Yahya son of Zakariyya (peace be upon them both) a believer in his mother's belly, and created Pharaoh a disbeliever in his mother's belly. > **[""Allah created Yahya son of Zakariyya a believer in his mother's belly, and created Pharaoh a disbeliever in his mother's belly""]**"
"11812","Abdullah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both) said he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say Allah created His creation in darkness, then cast upon them of His light; whom it reached that day was guided, whom it missed strayed. Hence he says the Pen has dried upon Allah's knowledge. > **[""Indeed Allah created His creation in darkness, then cast upon them of His light; whomsoever His light reached that day was guided, and whomsoever it missed strayed; therefore I say: the Pen has dried upon the knowledge of Allah""]**"
"11813","In another narration the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said Allah created His creation, placed them in darkness, took what He willed of His light and cast it upon them; it reached whom He willed and missed whom He willed. Hence he says the Pen has dried. > **[""The Pen has dried concerning what shall be""]**"
"11814","Abdullah ibn Masud (may Allah be pleased with him) reported they were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a rider arrived after nine nights travel, exhausted body, sleepless nights, thirsty days, to ask two matters depriving sleep. Asked his name, he said Zayd of Horses, so he named him Zayd of Good. He asked Allah's mark in whom He wants and in whom He does not, loving good and grieving loss; he was told preparation for the other abode is the sign. > **[""What is your name""]** > **[""I am Zayd of Horses""]** > **[""Rather you are Zayd of Good""]** > **[""It is the mark of Allah in whom He wants and the mark of Allah in whom He does not want; had He wanted you for the other, He would have prepared you for it, then He would not care in which valley you perished""]**"
"11815","Abu Bakr the Truthful (may Allah be pleased with him) said he asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) whether they act upon a finished matter or a new one. He said upon what is finished. Asked why act, he said each is facilitated. > **[""Upon a matter already finished""]** > **[""Each is facilitated for what he was created for""]**"
"11816","Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) whether their deeds concern what is finished or a new beginning. He said what is finished. Umar asked whether to rely, and he commanded action, for the happy work happiness and the wretched work wretchedness. > **[""It concerns what has been finished""]** > **[""Act, O son of Khattab, for each is facilitated; whoever is among the happy works for happiness, and whoever is among the wretched works for wretchedness""]**"
"11817","Abu al-Darda (may Allah be pleased with him) reported people asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) whether their deeds concern a finished matter or something new. He said a finished matter. Asked how then to act, he said each is prepared for what he was created for. > **[""Rather a matter already finished""]** > **[""Each is prepared for what he was created for""]**"
"11818","Dhu al-Lihyah al-Kilabi (may Allah be pleased with him) asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) whether they act in a new matter or one already finished. He said in one already finished. Asked why act, he commanded action, for each is facilitated. > **[""No, rather in a matter already finished""]** > **[""Act, for each is facilitated for what he was created for""]**"
"11819","Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) reported that Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) whether their deeds concern what is finished or new. He said what is finished. Asked why act, he said each is facilitated. > **[""Rather something already finished""]** > **[""Each is facilitated for what he was created for""]**"
"11820","Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) reported a man asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) whether they act according to flowing measures and a dried Pen or something new. He said according to flowing measures and dried Pen. Asked why act, he commanded action. > **[""Rather according to what the measures have flowed with and the Pen has dried upon""]** > **[""Act, for each is facilitated for what he was created for""]**"
"11821","Jabir ibn Abdillah (may Allah be pleased with them both) reported that Suraqah ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) stood before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked whether their deeds incur reckoning good for good and evil for evil, or measures preceded and pens dried. He said measures preceded. Asked on what to act, he commanded action, and Suraqah resolved to strive. > **[""O Suraqah, the measures have preceded concerning it and the pens have dried concerning it""]** > **[""Act, O Suraqah, for every worker is facilitated for what he was created for""]**"
"11822","Suraqah ibn Malik ibn Jushum al-Mudliji (may Allah be pleased with him) asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) whether they act upon what is finished or begin anew. He said for a finished deed. Asked why act, he said each is facilitated his deed, then stressed earnestness twice. > **[""Rather for a deed already finished""]** > **[""Each is facilitated his deed""]** > **[""Now earnestness, now earnestness""]**"
"11823","Abu al-Darda (may Allah be pleased with him) said he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say Allah has finished for each servant five: his term, provision, trace, resting place, and in one narration his deed. > **[""Allah has finished for each servant five: his term, his provision, his trace, his resting place, and his deed""]**"
"11824","Abdullah ibn Masud (may Allah be pleased with him) said four are finished: creation, character, provision and term; none earns more than another. He added that charity is valid whether taken possession of or not. > **[""Four are finished: creation, character, provision and term; none is a greater earner than another""]**"
"11825","Abdullah ibn Masud (may Allah be pleased with him) reported from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that four are finished for the son of Adam: creation, character, provision and term. > **[""Four are finished for the son of Adam: creation, character, provision and term""]**"
"11826","Abu al-Darda (may Allah be pleased with him) reported that increase of lifespan was mentioned before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who recited the meaning that Allah never delays a soul when its term arrives, then continued the narration. > **[""Allah never delays a soul when its term arrives""]**"
"11827","Abu al-Darda (may Allah be pleased with him) reported they were discussing future events when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to believe a mountain moved if heard, but not to believe a man abandoned his inborn character, for he returns to what he was fashioned upon. > **[""When you hear that a mountain has moved from its place, believe it; and when you hear that a man has departed from his character, do not believe it, for he shall return to what he was fashioned upon""]**"
"11828","Abdullah ibn Rabiah reported they were with Abdullah ibn Masud (may Allah be pleased with him) when people mentioned a man's character. He asked whether cutting his head, hand or foot could be restored; they said no. He concluded they cannot change his character till they change his creation. > **[""Do you think if you cut off his head you could restore it? Could you restore his hand? His foot? Then you cannot change his character until you change his creation""]**"
"11829","Abu Urwah (may Allah be pleased with him) reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said when Allah wills to take a servant's soul in a land, He assigns him a need toward it, and when he reaches his farthest trace, He takes him. > **[""When Allah wills to take His servant in a land, He assigns him a need toward it; when he reaches his farthest trace, He takes him""]**"
"11830","From Abu Urwah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said when Allah wills to take a servant in a land He makes for him a need there that does not end till he arrives. Then he recited the end of Surah Luqman on the Hour, rain, wombs and souls, sealed it, and said these are the keys of the unseen known only to Allah. > **[""When Allah wills to take a servant in a land, He makes for him a need there, and it does not end until he comes to it""]** > **[""These are the keys of the unseen; none knows them but Allah""]**"
"11831","Usamah ibn Zayd (may Allah be pleased with them both) reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said no servant's death is appointed in a land except that a need is made for him therein. > **[""No servant's death is appointed in a land except that a need is made for him therein""]**"
"11832","Hudhayfah (may Allah be pleased with him) reported from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that Allah created every maker and his making. > **[""Allah created every maker and his making""]**"
"11833","Abu al-Darda (may Allah be pleased with him) reported from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that everything has a reality, and no servant reaches the reality of faith till he knows what struck him could not have missed him and what missed him could not have struck him. > **[""Everything has a reality, and no servant reaches the reality of faith until he knows that what struck him could not have missed him, and what missed him could not have struck him""]**"
"11834","Abdullah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both) reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said a person does not believe till he believes in decree, its good and evil. > **[""A person does not believe until he believes in decree, its good and its evil""]**"
"11835","Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said all matters, good and evil, are from Allah, and decree is the system of oneness; whoever affirms Allah and believes in decree holds the firmest handle. > **[""All matters, their good and evil, are from Allah""]** > **[""Decree is the system of oneness; whoever affirms Allah and believes in decree has held to the firmest handle""]**"
"11836","Amr ibn Shuayb reported he sat with Said ibn al-Musayyib when a man said Allah decreed all but deeds, provoking intense anger. Said then related from Rafi ibn Khadij (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) warned of a people in his nation disbelieving Allah and Quran unknowingly like Jews and Christians, affirming part of decree and denying part, saying good is from Allah and evil from Iblis, incurring enmity, tyranny, plague, sinking, transformation and the Dajjal; he wept in mercy though among them are worshippers, and taught true faith in decree. > **[""There shall be a people in my nation who disbelieve in Allah and the Quran while unaware, as the Jews and Christians disbelieved""]** > **[""They affirm part of decree and deny part of it""]** > **[""They say: good is from Allah and evil is from Iblis""]** > **[""Believe in Allah alone, that none besides Him owns harm or benefit; believe in Paradise and Fire; know Allah created them before creation, then placed whom He willed in Paradise and whom He willed in Fire as justice from Him; each works for what was finished for him and shall end at what was finished for him""]**"
"11837","Al-Walid ibn Ubadah reported that when Ubadah (may Allah be pleased with him) neared death, his son Abd al-Rahman asked counsel. Seated upright, he enjoined fear of Allah, which requires faith in Allah, which requires faith in decree good and evil and certainty that what struck could not miss, citing the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). > **[""O my son, fear Allah; you shall not fear Allah until you believe in Allah, and you shall not believe in Allah until you believe in decree, its good and evil, and that what struck you could not have missed you, and what missed you could not have struck you""]** > **[""Decree is upon this; whoever dies upon other than it enters the Fire""]**"
"11838","In another narration Ubadah (may Allah be pleased with him) added that one does not taste faith nor reach true knowledge of Allah till believing in decree. > **[""He has not tasted the taste of faith, and you shall not reach the reality of knowledge of Allah until you believe in decree""]**"
"11839","Abu al-Aswad al-Duali reported he asked Imran ibn Husayn, Abdullah ibn Masud and Ubayy ibn Kab (may Allah be pleased with them) about decree after disputing deniers till expelled. They answered that if Allah punished heaven and earth He would not wrong, His mercy is wider than sins, but He decreed to punish and mercy whom He wills in truth, and even Uhud-like gold spent in Allah's path is rejected till one believes in decree good and evil. Imran said he heard it from the Prophet with the other two present. > **[""Had Allah punished the folk of heaven and earth He would have punished them without wronging, and had He admitted them into His mercy His mercy would be wider than their sins; but He decreed as He said: He punishes whom He wills and mercies whom He wills; whom He punishes is justice, and whom He mercies is justice; had you gold like Uhud to spend in Allah's path, it would not be accepted till you believe in decree, its good and evil""]**"
"11840","Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan (may Allah be pleased with them both) reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade hastening toward what one thinks attainable if Allah did not decree it, or holding back from what one thinks avoidable if Allah decreed it upon him. > **[""Do not hasten toward a thing thinking that by hastening you shall attain it if Allah did not decree it; nor hold back from a thing thinking that by holding back it shall be repelled from you if Allah decreed it upon you""]**"
"11841","Al-Harith reported he saw Ibn Masud (may Allah be pleased with him) moisten his finger in his mouth then swear that no servant finds faith's taste till believing in decree and knowing he shall die then be raised after death. > **[""By Allah, no servant finds the taste of faith until he believes in decree, and knows that he shall die then be raised after death""]**"
"11842","Abu al-Hajjaj al-Azdi said he heard Salman al-Farisi (may Allah be pleased with him) at Isfahan say no servant believes till knowing what struck him could not miss him and what missed him could not strike him. > **[""No servant believes until he knows that what struck him could not have missed him, and what missed him could not have struck him""]**"
"11843","Amr ibn al-As (may Allah be pleased with him) reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came, stood over them, and said past nations perished by questioning their prophets and differing over them, and none believes till believing in decree good and evil. > **[""Those before you perished only by questioning their prophets and differing over them; none shall believe until he believes in decree, its good and evil""]**"
"11844","Amir al-Shabi reported that Adi ibn Hatim (may Allah be pleased with him) came to Kufa, and youths among Kufa scholars asked a Prophetic narration. He said he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to submit, was told to submit and be safe, asked what Islam is, and was told testimony and faith in all decrees sweet bitter. > **[""O Adi ibn Hatim, submit and be safe""]** > **[""Bear witness none is worthy of worship but Allah, bear witness I am Allah's Messenger, and believe in all decrees, their good and evil, sweet and bitter""]**"
"11845","Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) reported that when Allah sent Musa (peace be upon him) with the Torah, Musa asked how the Great Lord who could enforce obedience is yet disobeyed though He loves obedience. Allah answered He is not questioned while they are questioned, so Musa desisted. Uzayr, after the Torah was lifted then restored till some claimed he was Allah's son, repeated the question thrice; Allah asked whether he could bundle sunlight, measure wind or weigh light, warned likewise, and erased his name from among Prophets though a prophet. When Isa (peace be upon him), honored with Book, wisdom, Torah, Gospel and miracles, asked likewise, Allah reminded him he is servant, messenger, word cast to Maryam, spirit from Him, created from dust by Be, warned as his predecessor, so Isa told followers decree is Allah's veil. > **[""O Allah, You are a Great Lord; had You willed to be obeyed You would be obeyed, and had You willed not to be disobeyed You would not be disobeyed; yet You love to be obeyed while You are disobeyed, so how is this, my Lord""]** > **[""I am not questioned about what I do, while they are questioned""]** > **[""Can you bundle a bundle of sunlight? Can you bring a measure of wind? Can you bring a weight of light? Likewise you cannot grasp what you asked about""]** > **[""Decree is Allah's veil, so do not burden yourselves with it""]**"
"11846","Said ibn Jubayr reported that the Children of Israil asked Musa (peace be upon him) whether his Lord creates people then punishes them. Allah inspired him to sow, reap, then winnow till chaff remained, asked its use, and answered like chaff for fire He punishes only who deserves Fire. > **[""Sow, so he sowed; then He said: reap, so he reaped; then He said: winnow, so he winnowed, and chaff remained; He said: for what is this fit? He said: for fire; He said: likewise I punish none of My creation except who deserves the Fire""]**"
"11847","Wahb ibn Munabbih said he accompanied Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) before and after his blindness, and when asked about decree Ibn Abbas said the boldest speaker is most ignorant, the weakest most knowledgeable, and pondering it is like gazing at sunlight, more gazing brings more bewilderment. > **[""I found the boldest of people in speaking about it the most ignorant of it, and the weakest in speaking about it the most knowledgeable of it; I found one pondering it like one gazing at the sun's rays: the more he gazes, the more his sight grows bewildered""]**"
"11848","Thawban (may Allah be pleased with him) reported forty Companions including Abu Bakr and Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) debated decree and compulsion, whereupon Jibril the Trustworthy descended commanding Muhammad to go out for his nation innovated. He came at an unusual hour, complexion glowing, cheeks flushed as if bursting with sour pomegranate, so they rose baring arms trembling and repented. > **[""O Muhammad, go out to your nation, for they have innovated""]** > **[""Woe to you, if you persist you shall incur""]**"
"11849","Abu al-Darda, Wathilah ibn al-Asqa, Abu Umamah and Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with them) said they debated decree in a Jewish gathering when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came angry, frowned, rebuked, warned of two deep dark valleys and stirring fire's blaze, ordered the Jews to rise, spread his right then left announcing books of Paradise and Fire thrice finished, and took witness he conveyed. > **[""Quiet! Fear Allah, O nation of Muhammad; two deep yawning dark valleys; do not stir upon yourselves the blaze of Fire""]** > **[""In the Name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful: this is a book from the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful, with names of Paradise folk and names of their fathers, mothers and clans; your Lord has finished, your Lord has finished, your Lord has finished""]** > **[""In the Name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful: this is a book from the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful, with names of Fire folk and names of their fathers, mothers and clans; your Lord has finished, your Lord has finished, your Lord has finished""]** > **[""Have I excused? Have I warned? O Allah, I have conveyed""]**"
"11850","Thawban (may Allah be pleased with him) reported from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that when his Companions are mentioned withhold, when the stars are mentioned withhold, and when decree is mentioned withhold. > **[""When my Companions are mentioned, withhold; when the stars are mentioned, withhold; and when decree is mentioned, withhold""]**"
"11851","Abdullah ibn Masud (may Allah be pleased with him) reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said when his Companions are mentioned withhold, when the stars are mentioned withhold, and when decree is mentioned withhold. > **[""When my Companions are mentioned, withhold; when the stars are mentioned, withhold; and when decree is mentioned, withhold""]**"
"11852","Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: > **""Beware of Qadar, for it is a branch of Christianity.""**"
"11853","Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came out from the door of the house intending the chamber, and heard people disputing about Qadar, saying, did not Allah say such and such, did not Allah reveal such and such verse. The narrator said, the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, opened the chamber door, and it was as if pomegranate seeds had been burst open upon his face from anger, and he said: > **""Were you commanded with this, or was this intended for you. Those before you perished only through the like of this. They struck parts of the Book of Allah against other parts. What Allah commanded you, follow it, and what He forbade you, refrain from it.""** The narrator said, after that no one was heard speaking about it, until Mabad al-Juhani, then al-Hajjaj seized him and killed him."
"11854","Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, with doubt over one word meaning concordant or near: > **""The affair of this Ummah will remain harmonious and close so long as they do not speak about children and Qadar.""**"
"11855","Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: > **""The last speech about Qadar will belong to the worst of this Ummah.""** In another wording: > **""To the worst of my Ummah in the akhir al-zaman.""**"
"11856","Abu al-Darda, may Allah be pleased with him, reported from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: > **""No disobedient to parents, no habitual drinker of wine, and no denier of Qadar shall enter Paradise.""** In another wording is added: > **""Nor one who reminds others of his favors.""**"
"11857","Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, said, I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: > **""There shall be maskh in this Ummah. Know that it shall be among the deniers of Qadar and the Zanadiqah.""**"
"11858","Nafi reported, while we were sitting with Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, a man came and said, so-and-so, a man of Sham, conveys salam to you. Ibn Umar, may Allah have mercy on him, said, it has reached me that he has innovated an affair, so if that is so, do not convey my salam to him. I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: > **""There shall be in my Ummah maskh and qadhf, and it shall be among the people of zandaqah.""**"
"11859","Sahl ibn Sad al-Saidi, may Allah be pleased with him, reported from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: > **""There was never zandaqah except preceded by denial of Qadar.""**"
"11860","Jabir ibn Samurah, may Allah be pleased with him, said, I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: > **""Three things I fear for my Ummah: seeking rain by the stars, oppression of the ruler, and denial of Qadar.""**"
"11861","Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: > **""I fear for my Ummah five things: denial of Qadar and belief in the stars.""** Two of the five were mentioned in brevity."
"11862","Abu Umamah, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: > **""The most fearful of what I fear for my Ummah in its last age is the stars, denial of Qadar, and oppression of the ruler.""**"
"11863","Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: > **""The ruin of my Ummah is in three: tribal partisanship, Qadariyyah, and narration without verification.""**"
"11864","Abu al-Darda, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: > **""I fear for my Ummah three things: the slip of the scholar, the argument of the hypocrite by the Quran, and denial of Qadar.""**"
"11865","Abu Musa al-Ashari, may Allah be pleased with him, said, Qadar was mentioned before the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: > **""My Ummah shall remain holding fast to its religion so long as they do not deny Qadar. When they deny Qadar, then their ruin comes.""**"
"11866","Abu Umamah, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: > **""There was no shirk since Allah sent Adam, upon him be peace, from heaven to earth except that its beginning was denial of Qadar. No Ummah committed shirk except through denial of Qadar. You, O Ummah, shall be tested with it. When you meet them, you be the questioners, and do not give them room to question, lest they cast doubts upon you.""**"
"11867","Abdullah ibn Amr, may Allah be pleased with them both, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: > **""No Ummah ever perished except through belief in the stars, and the beginning of its shirk was only denial of Qadar.""** In another wording: > **""No Ummah ever perished until it associated partners with Allah, and no Ummah associated partners with Allah until the first of its shirk was denial of Qadar.""**"
"11868","Muadh ibn Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: > **""Allah never sent a prophet except that in his Ummah were Qadariyyah and Murjiah who confuse the affair of his Ummah. Know, Allah has cursed the Qadariyyah and the Murjiah upon the tongues of seventy prophets.""**"
"11869","Muhammad ibn Ubayd reported from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that it was said to Ibn Abbas, a man has come to us who denies Qadar. He said, guide me to him, and he was then blind. It was said, what will you do with him, O Ibn Abbas. He said: > **""By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, if I gain power over him I shall bite his nose until I sever it, and if his neck falls into my hand I shall crush it. For I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: It is as if I see the women of Banu Fihr circling around al-Khazraj, their buttocks shaking, as mushrikat. This is the first shirk of this Ummah. By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, their excesses shall end with them expelling Allah from having decreed good, just as they expelled Him from having decreed evil.""**"
"11870","Said ibn Jubayr reported, I was in a circle in which was Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, and we mentioned Qadar. Ibn Abbas became intensely angry and said, if I knew among the people one of them I would seize him. I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: > **""Allah never sent a prophet then took him except that He placed after him a fatrah, and filled Hell from that fatrah.""** In another addition: > **""And they are the Qadariyyah.""**"
"11871","Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, said: > **""Allah never sent a prophet except that after him was a pause with which Hell shall be filled.""**"
"11872","Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, said, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me: > **""Perhaps you shall remain after me until you meet a people who deny the Qadar of Allah and attribute sins to His servants. They derived that speech from Christianity. When that happens, declare disavowal to Allah from them.""** Ibn Abbas used to raise his hands and say: > **""O Allah, I declare disavowal to You from them, as Your Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded.""**"
"11873","Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: > **""The Qadariyyah and the Murjiah are the Majus of this Ummah. If they fall ill, do not visit them, and if they die, do not attend them.""**"
"11874","Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: > **""The Qadariyyah are the Majus of this Ummah. If they fall ill, do not visit them, and if they die, do not attend them.""**"
"11875","Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: > **""Allah has cursed the people of Qadar, those who deny part of Qadar and affirm part of Qadar.""**"
"11876","Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: > **""Six I have cursed, and every answered prophet has cursed: one who adds to the Book of Allah, one who denies the Qadar of Allah, one who permits the prohibitions of Allah, one who permits from my kindred what Allah forbade, and one who abandons the Sunnah.""**"
"11877","Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, reported that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: > **""Whoever denies Qadar has denied what was revealed to Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him.""**"
"11878","Muhammad ibn Kab al-Qurazi said, the Qadariyyah were mentioned before Abdullah ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, and Abdullah ibn Umar said: > **""The Qadariyyah were cursed upon the tongues of seventy prophets and our Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. When the Day of Resurrection comes and Allah gathers people on one plain, a caller who makes the first and last hear shall call: Where are the adversaries of Allah. Then the Qadariyyah shall rise.""**"
"11879","Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: > **""When the Day of Resurrection comes, a caller shall call: Let the adversaries of Allah rise, and they are the Qadariyyah.""**"
"11880","Abu Said al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: > **""In the akhir al-zaman a woman shall come and find her husband transformed into a monkey, because he did not believe in Qadar.""**"
"11881","Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: > **""Whoever does not believe in Qadar, its good and its evil, I am free of him.""**"
"11882","Sahl ibn Sad, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: > **""No servant believes until he believes in Qadar.""**"
"11883","Abu Umamah, may Allah be pleased with him, reported from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: > **""Four Allah shall not look at on the Day of Resurrection: disobedient to parents, one who reminds of favors, habitual drinker of wine, and denier of Qadar.""**"
"11884","In a narration: > **""Three from whom Allah accepts neither sarf nor adl.""** Then he mentioned the like thereof."
"11885","Wathilah ibn al-Asqa, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: > **""Two groups of this Ummah my intercession shall not reach: the Murjiah and the Qadariyyah.""**"
"11886","Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: > **""Two groups of my Ummah my intercession shall not reach: the Murjiah and the Qadariyyah.""**"
"11887","Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: > **""Two groups of my Ummah have no share in Islam: the Murjiah and the Qadariyyah.""**"
"11888","Abu Said, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: > **""Two groups of my Ummah have no share in Islam: the Murjiah and the Qadariyyah.""**"
"11889","Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: > **""Two groups of my Ummah shall not come to me at the Hawd nor enter Paradise: the Qadariyyah and the Murjiah.""**"
"11890","Sahl ibn Sad al-Saidi, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: > **""Every Ummah has Majus, every Ummah has Christians, every Ummah has Jews. The Majus of my Ummah are the Qadariyyah, their Christians are the Hashwiyyah, and their Jews are the Murjiah.""**"
"11891","Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: > **""Whoever is not pleased with the decree of Allah and does not believe in His Qadar, let him seek a god other than Allah.""**"
"11892","Abu Hind al-Dari, may Allah be pleased with him, said, I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say, Allah, Blessed and Exalted is He, said: > **""Whoever is not pleased with My decree and is not patient with My trial, let him seek a lord other than Me.""**"
"11893","Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, said, Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, addressed us, praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: > **""After you there shall be a people who deny stoning, deny the Dajjal, deny intercession, deny punishment of the grave, and deny that a people shall exit the Fire after being charred.""** In an addition: > **""And they shall deny the rising of the sun from its west.""**"
"11894","Ibn Awn said: > **""I saw Ghaylan al-Qadari crucified at the gate of Damascus.""**"
"11895","Hammad ibn Zayd mentioned the Jahmiyyah and said: > **""They only attempt to claim there is nothing above the heaven.""**"
"11896","Abdullah, meaning Ibn Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, said: > **""For one of you to grasp a coal until it cools is better for him than to say about an affair Allah decreed: If only it had not been.""**"
"11897","Abu Umamah, may Allah be pleased with him, heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while riding al-Jadaa with al-Fadl ibn Abbas behind him, say: > **""Do not swear decisively upon Allah, do not swear decisively upon Allah, for whoever swears decisively upon Allah, Allah shall belie him.""**"
"11898","Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, said, disputation about Qadar took place before the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he disliked it intensely until it was as if pomegranate seeds had been burst upon his face. He said: > **""In what are you engaged.""** They said, we disputed about Qadar, O Messenger of Allah. He said: > **""Everything is by qada and qadar, even this.""** And he struck with his forefinger upon the cord of his other forearm."
"11899","Al-Dahhak ibn Muzahim said, I gathered with Tawus al-Yamani, Amr ibn Dinar, Makhul al-Shami, and al-Hasan al-Basri in Masjid al-Khayf, and we discussed Qadar until our voices rose and our clamor increased. Tawus stood and said, be silent, I shall inform you what I heard Abu al-Darda, may Allah be pleased with him, report from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: > **""Allah has obligated duties upon you, so do not neglect them. He has set limits, so do not transgress them. He forbade you things, so do not violate them. He remained silent about things without forgetfulness, so do not burden yourselves with them, as mercy from your Lord, so accept it. All affairs are in the Hand of Allah. From Allah is their origin, and to Him is their return. Servants have in them neither delegation nor will apart from Allah.""** Then the people all stood, pleased with what Tawus said."
"11900","Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, said, we said, O Messenger of Allah, horses run swiftly from us or shy away. One speaker said, O Messenger of Allah, was this in the prior Book. He said: > **""Yes.""**"
"11901","Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, from what Uthman ibn Umar knew, reported that a Jew saw in a dream: what a good people is the Ummah of Muhammad, were it not that they say, what Allah wills and Muhammad wills. That was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: > **""Do not say: What Allah wills and Muhammad wills. Say: What Allah wills alone.""**"
"11902","Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, reported from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: > **""Birds move by Qadar.""**"
"11903","Abu Umamah, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: > **""Entrusted with the believer are one hundred ninety angels repelling from him what was not decreed upon him. Of that, nine angels for the sight repelling from him as you repel flies from a bowl of honey on a hot day. If they were shown to you, you would see them over mountain and plain, each stretching his hand and opening his mouth. If the servant were entrusted to himself for a blink of an eye, the devils would snatch him.""**"
"11904","Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: > **""No caution avails against Qadar. Dua avails what the decree has not descended upon. Trial and dua meet between heaven and earth and contend until the Day of Resurrection.""**"
"11905","Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: > **""No caution avails against Qadar. Dua avails, I think he said, so long as Qadar has not descended. Dua meets trial and they contend until the Day of Resurrection.""**"
"11906","Sad ibn Abi Waqqas, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: > **""I wonder at the decree of Allah, Glorified is He, for the believer. If good befalls him, he praises his Lord and thanks. If calamity befalls him, he praises his Lord and is patient. The believer is rewarded in everything, even the morsel he raises to the mouth of his wife.""**"
"11907","Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: > **""I wonder at the believer. Allah, the Exalted, decrees no decree for the believer except that it is good for him.""**"
"11908","Abdullah ibn Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: > **""Allah, Mighty and Majestic is He, forbade no sanctity except that He knew some intruder among you would look into it. Know, I hold your waistbands lest you fall into the Fire like the falling of moths or flies.""** In another wording: > **""Moths, or flies, or beetles.""**"
"11909","Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: > **""When Allah intends to deviate the heart of a servant, He blinds him to means.""**"
"11910","Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, said, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, never raised his head to heaven except that he said: > **""O Turner of hearts, make my heart firm upon Your obedience.""**"
"11911","Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, reported that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to supplicate: > **""O Turner of hearts, make my heart firm upon Your religion.""** Aishah said, I said, may my father and mother be ransom for you, O Messenger of Allah, do you fear while you are the Messenger of Allah. He said: > **""O Aishah, the hearts of the children of Adam are between two fingers of the fingers of the Most Merciful. Whomever He wills to turn from misguidance to guidance, or from guidance to misguidance, He does.""**"
"11912","Umm Salamah, may Allah be pleased with her, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, often said in his dua: > **""O Allah, Turner of hearts, make my heart firm upon Your religion.""** She said, I said, O Messenger of Allah, do hearts indeed turn. He said: > **""Yes. There is no human of the children of Adam except that his heart is between two fingers of the fingers of Allah, Mighty and Majestic is He. If He wills He keeps it straight, and if He wills He deviates it. So we ask Allah not to deviate our hearts after He guided us, and we ask Him to grant us mercy from Himself. He is the Bestower.""**"
"11913","Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: > **""The heart of the son of Adam is only between two fingers of the fingers of the Most Merciful.""**"
"11914","Nuaym ibn Hammar al-Ghatafani, may Allah be pleased with him, said, I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: > **""There is no human except that his heart is between two fingers of the fingers of the Most Merciful. If He wills to deviate it He deviates it, and if He wills to keep it straight He keeps it straight. Each day the Balance is in the Hand of Allah. He raises peoples and lowers others until the Day of Resurrection.""**"
"11915","Samurah ibn Fatik al-Asadi, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: > **""The Balance is in the Hand of Allah. He raises peoples and lowers peoples. The heart of the son of Adam is between two fingers of the fingers of the Most Merciful. If He wills He deviates it, and if He wills He keeps it straight.""**"
"11916","Al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad, may Allah be pleased with him, said, I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: > **""The heart of the son of Adam turns more quickly than a pot when it boils fully.""**"
"11917","Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: > **""You need not admire anyone until you see with what he is sealed. A worker works a time of his life with righteous work, such that if he died upon it he would enter Paradise, then he turns and works evil work. A servant works a time with evil work, such that if he died upon it he would enter the Fire, then he turns and works righteous work. When Allah, Blessed and Exalted is He, intends good for a servant, He employs him before his death.""** They said, O Messenger of Allah, how does He employ him. He said: > **""He grants him success to righteous work, then takes his soul upon it.""**"
"11918","Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: > **""A man works the work of the people of Paradise, while he is written in the Book among the people of the Fire, then before his death he turns and works the work of the people of the Fire and dies and enters it. A man works the work of the people of the Fire, while he is written in the Book among the people of Paradise, then before his death he turns and works the work of the people of Paradise and dies and enters it.""**"
"11919","Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, said, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came out to us grasping something in his hand. He opened his right hand and said: > **""In the Name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate. This is a book from the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate, in it are the people of Paradise with their numbers, names, and lineages, totaled until the Day of Resurrection. None shall be decreased from them nor increased among them. The fortunate may be led the path of wretchedness until it is said he is of them, how he resembles them, then he is moved to his felicity before his death, even in the time of milking a she-camel.""** Then he opened his left hand and said: > **""In the Name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate. This is a book from the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate, in it are the people of the Fire with their numbers and names, totaled until the Day of Resurrection. None shall be decreased from them nor increased among them. The wretched may be led the path of felicity until it is said he is of them, how he resembles them, then his wretchedness overtakes him before his death, even in the time of milking a she-camel.""** Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said thrice: > **""Works are by their seals.""**"
"11920","Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, reported from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: > **""A man works, or he said, does the work of the people of the Fire for seventy years, then he is sealed with the work of the people of Paradise. A worker works seventy years with the work of the people of Paradise, then he is sealed with the work of the people of the Fire.""**"
"11921","Al-Urs ibn Umayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: > **""A servant works a time with the work of the people of the Fire, then a highway of the highways of Paradise appears before him, and he works with it until he dies upon it, and that is for what was written for him. A man works a time with the work of the people of Paradise, then a highway of the highways of the Fire appears before him, and he works with it until he dies upon it, and that is for what was written for him.""**"
"11922","Abdullah ibn Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: > **""A servant is born a believer, lives a believer, and dies a believer. A servant is born a disbeliever, lives a disbeliever, and dies a disbeliever. A servant works a time with felicity, then what was written for him overtakes him and he dies a disbeliever. A servant works a time with wretchedness, then what was written for him overtakes him and he dies fortunate.""**"
"11923","Abdullah ibn Amr, may Allah be pleased with them both, reported from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: > **""A servant is written a believer for ages upon ages, then he dies while Allah is angry with him. A servant is written a disbeliever for ages upon ages, then he dies while Allah is pleased with him. Whoever dies as a slanderer, backbiter, and nicknamer of people, his mark on the Day of Resurrection shall be that Allah brands him upon the nose from both lips.""**"
"11924","Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ascended the minbar, praised Allah and extolled Him, and said: > **""A book Allah wrote, in it are the people of Paradise with their names and lineages, totaled, neither increased nor decreased until the Day of Resurrection. The companion of Paradise is sealed with the work of the people of Paradise, and the companion of the Fire is sealed with the work of the people of the Fire, whatever work he does. The fortunate may be led the path of the wretched until it is said how he resembles them, indeed he is of them, then felicity reaches them and rescues them. The wretched may be led the path of the fortunate until it is said how he resembles them, indeed he is of them, then wretchedness overtakes them. Whomever Allah wrote fortunate in the Mother of the Book, He shall not take him from the world until He employs him with work that makes him fortunate before his death, even in the time of milking a she-camel.""** Then he said thrice: > **""Works are by their seals.""**"
"11925","Kab ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said of a man: > **""He is of the people of the Fire.""** People awaited his affair, until on the day of Hunayn the man fought fiercely. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was informed, and said: > **""He is of the people of the Fire.""** The man took an arrow from his quiver and slaughtered himself. They said, O Messenger of Allah, Allah has confirmed your speech. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: > **""Rise and proclaim: None shall enter Paradise except a believer. Allah supports this religion even with a wicked man.""**"
"11926","Aktham ibn Abi al-Jawn, may Allah be pleased with him, said, we said, O Messenger of Allah, so-and-so advances in fighting. He said: > **""He is of the people of the Fire.""** We said, O Messenger of Allah, if so-and-so with his worship, striving, and gentleness is in the Fire, where are we. He said: > **""That is the humility of hypocrisy, and he is in the Fire.""** We watched him in fighting. No horseman nor footman passed him except that he attacked him, and his wounds increased. We came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said, O Messenger of Allah, so-and-so was martyred. He said: > **""He is in the Fire.""** When the pain of wounds intensified, he took his sword, placed it between his breasts, leaned upon it until it exited his back. I came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said, I bear witness you are the Messenger of Allah. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: > **""A man works the work of the people of Paradise while he is of the people of the Fire. A man works the work of the people of the Fire while he is of the people of Paradise. Wretchedness and felicity overtake him at the departure of his soul, and he is sealed with it.""**"
"11927","Abu Umamah, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: > **""Do not admire the work of a worker until you see with what he is sealed.""**"
"11928","Abdur Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Kab ibn Malik reported from one who witnessed the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, at Khaybar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said of a man with him: > **""He is of the people of the Fire.""** When fighting came the man fought fiercely until wounds increased. Men of the Companions, may Allah be pleased with them, said, O Messenger of Allah, the man you mentioned as of the Fire fought fiercely in the path of Allah and was much wounded. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: > **""He is of the people of the Fire.""** Some people almost doubted. Then the man felt pain of wounds, reached to his quiver, took an arrow, and killed himself with it. A Muslim hastened to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said, O Messenger of Allah, Allah has confirmed your word, so-and-so slaughtered himself."
"11929","Amr ibn al-Hamiq al-Khuzai, may Allah be pleased with him, heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: > **""When Allah intends good for a servant, He employs him before his death.""** It was said, how does He employ him. He said: > **""Righteous work is opened for him before his death until those around him are pleased with him.""**"
"11930","Jubayr ibn Nufayr reported that Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: > **""When Allah intends good for a servant, He employs him before his death.""** A man asked, how does He employ him. He said: > **""Allah, Blessed and Exalted is He, guides him to righteous work before his death, then takes his soul upon it.""**"
"11931","Abu Anbah reported that Shurayh ibn al-Numan, may Allah be pleased with him, who had companionship, said that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: > **""When Allah intends good for a servant, He honeys him.""** It was said, what is His honeying him. He said: > **""He opens for him righteous work before his death, then takes him upon it.""**"
"11932","Abu Umamah, may Allah be pleased with him, said, I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: > **""When Allah intends good for a servant, He purifies him before his death.""** They said, O Messenger of Allah, what is the purification of the servant. He said: > **""Righteous work He inspires him with until He takes him upon it.""** In some paths the word honeyed came in place of purified."
"11933","Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: > **""When Allah intends good for a servant, He washes him.""** It was said, O Messenger of Allah, how does He wash him. He said: > **""He grants him success to righteous work before his death, then takes him upon it.""**"
"11934","Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: > **""When Allah intends good for a servant, He employs him.""** Then he fell silent. They said, in what, O Messenger of Allah. He said: > **""He employs him with righteous work before he dies.""**"
"11935","Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, said, I leaned the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, to my chest, and he said: > **""Whoever says la ilaha illa Allah seeking the Face of Allah, sealed with it, shall enter Paradise. Whoever fasts a day seeking the Face of Allah, sealed with it, shall enter Paradise. Whoever gives charity seeking the Face of Allah, sealed with it, shall enter Paradise.""**"
"11936","Aswad ibn Sari, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: > **""Four shall argue on the Day of Resurrection: a deaf man who hears nothing, a foolish man, an aged man, and a man who died in the fatrah. The deaf shall say: Islam came and I heard nothing. The foolish shall say: O Lord, Islam came while children pelted me with dung. The aged shall say: O Lord, Islam came and I understood nothing. The one who died in the fatrah shall say: No messenger came to me from You.""** He shall take their covenant to obey Him, then send upon them: > **""Enter the Fire.""** By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, if they entered it, it would be coolness and peace upon them."
"11937","Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: > **""Four shall be brought on the Day of Resurrection: the newborn, the ma-tuh, one who died in the fatrah, and the decrepit old man. Each shall speak his plea. The Lord, Blessed and Exalted is He, shall say to a neck of the Fire: Emerge. Then He shall say to them: I sent to My servants messengers from themselves. I am My own messenger to you. Enter this.""** Whoever was written wretched shall say: > **""O Lord, where shall we enter it, when from it we fled.""** Of whoever was written fortunate, he said: > **""He shall proceed and plunge into it hastening.""** Then Allah, Blessed and Exalted is He, shall say: > **""You would have denied My messengers more intensely and disobeyed. He shall admit these to Paradise and these to the Fire.""**"
"11938","Abu Said, meaning al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, reported from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in his reckoning, that he said: > **""The perished in the fatrah, the ma-tuh, and the newborn shall be brought. The perished in the fatrah shall say: No book nor messenger came to me. The ma-tuh shall say: O Lord, You gave me no intellect to understand good or evil. The newborn shall say: I did not reach deeds.""** He said: > **""A fire shall be raised for them, and it shall be said to them: Return it, or he said: Enter it. Whoever in the knowledge of Allah was fortunate, had he reached deeds, shall enter it. Whoever in the knowledge of Allah was wretched, had he reached deeds, shall withhold from it.""** Then He, Blessed and Exalted is He, shall say: > **""Me you disobeyed, so how with My messengers in the unseen.""**"
"11939","Muadh ibn Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, reported from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: > **""On the Day of Resurrection shall be brought one deprived of intellect, one perished in the fatrah, and one perished young. The deprived of intellect shall say: O Lord, had You given me intellect, whoever You gave intellect would not be more fortunate with his intellect than me. The perished in the fatrah shall say: O Lord, had a covenant come to me from You, whoever received a covenant from You would not be more fortunate with his covenant than me. The perished young shall say: Had You given me age, whoever You gave age would not be more fortunate with his age than me.""** The Lord, Blessed and Exalted is He, shall say: > **""I command you a command, will you obey Me.""** They shall say: > **""Yes, by Your might.""** He shall say: > **""Go and enter the Fire.""** Had they entered it, it would not harm them. Flames shall emerge upon them, and they shall think it destroyed all Allah created, so they shall return hastening and say: > **""We came out, O Lord, intending to enter it, but flames emerged upon us, and we thought it destroyed all Allah created.""** He shall command them a second time, and they shall return likewise saying the like. Allah, Blessed and Exalted is He, shall say: > **""Before you were created I knew what you would do. Upon My knowledge I created you, and to My knowledge you return. The Fire shall seize them.""**"
"11940","Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said, Khadijah, may Allah be pleased with her, asked the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about two sons of hers who died in the Jahiliyyah. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: > **""They are in the Fire.""** When he saw dislike in her face, he said: > **""Had you seen their place, you would hate them more.""** She said, O Messenger of Allah, and my child from you. He said: > **""In Paradise.""** Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: > **""Muslims and their offspring are in Paradise. Mushriks and their offspring are in the Fire.""** Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, recited: Those who believed and their offspring followed them in faith, We joined their offspring with them, Surah al-Tur 21."
"11941","Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, mentioned the children of the mushriks to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: > **""If you wish, I shall make you hear their crying in the Fire.""**"
"11942","Khadijah, may Allah be pleased with her, said, I said, O Messenger of Allah, where are my children from you. He said: > **""In Paradise.""** I said, without work. He said: > **""Allah knows best what they would have done.""** I said, where are my children from before you. He said: > **""In the Fire.""** I said, without work. He said: > **""Allah knew what they would have done.""**"
"11943","Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, said, I used to say about the children of the mushriks that they are of them. A man narrated to me from a man of the Companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then I met him, and he narrated to me from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: > **""Their Lord knows best of them. He created them, and He knows best of them and what they would have done.""**"
"11944","In a narration, Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, said: > **""So I withheld my opinion.""**"
"11945","Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, said, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was in one of his expeditions. A man asked him, O Messenger of Allah, what do you say about the lahun. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was silent and did not answer him. When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, finished the expedition and went about, he saw a boy fallen playing with the earth. He called his crier: > **""Where is the questioner about the lahun.""** The man came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade killing children, then said: > **""Allah knows best what they would have done. This is of the lahun.""**"
"11946","Jabir ibn Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with them both, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: > **""Every newborn is born upon the fitrah until his tongue expresses from him. When his tongue expresses, then either grateful or ungrateful.""**"
"11947","Samurah ibn Jundub, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: > **""Every newborn is born upon the fitrah, then his parents make him a Jew or a Christian.""**"
"11948","Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, reported that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: > **""Every newborn is born upon the fitrah, then his parents make him a Jew and make him a Christian.""**"
"11949","Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: > **""Every newborn is born upon the fitrah, then his parents make him a Jew and make him a Christian.""**"
"11950","Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, reported from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, as Musa ibn Wardan knew it with doubt, that he said: > **""The offspring of the Muslims are in Paradise. Ibrahim, upon him be peace, cares for them.""**"
"11951","Aswad ibn Sari, may Allah be pleased with him, said, it was said, O Messenger of Allah, who is in Paradise. He said: > **""The Prophet is in Paradise, the martyr is in Paradise, and the newborn is in Paradise.""**"
"11952","Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, reported that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was asked, who is in Paradise. He said: > **""The Prophet is in Paradise, the martyr is in Paradise, the newborn is in Paradise, and the buried alive girl is in Paradise.""**"
"11953","Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, reported from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: > **""The newborn is in Paradise, and the buried alive girl is in Paradise.""** He mentioned a third, and it escaped me."
"11954","Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: > **""I asked my Lord about the lahun of the offspring of mankind, that He not punish them, and He granted them to me.""** In a wording: > **""I asked Allah for the lahun of the offspring of mankind, and He granted them to me.""**"
"11955","Samurah ibn Jundub, may Allah be pleased with him, said, we asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about the children of the mushriks. He said: > **""They are servants of the people of Paradise.""**"
"11956","Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: > **""Children are servants of the people of Paradise.""** In the wording of two transmitters: > **""Children of the mushriks.""**"
